# Keep members out of their teammates' bullets (TMODE-38 CLEAR, BENCH-170; team thread "Stop friendly
# fire to close the team gap"). Team only: duel and melee fixtures replay bit for bit.
# The Ogi mirror (PR #569) showed our members take about 40 damage a round from our own bullets, Ogi's
# 11. Ogi fires with a mate in the line more often than we do but is hit 5x less per shot, so its
# members step out of the way. Ours check a teammate's bullet only 15 ticks ahead, from a standstill
# in any direction; a member running at 8 px a tick brakes and turns slowly, so it drives into the
# bullet it "dodged". CLEAR ranks only destinations whose drive (with Hadur's real heading, speed
# and turn rate, 40 ticks) meets no teammate bullet. Cloud (GrofGroup, DiamondStealers, 4 seeds each
# from 7400): own-fire damage 39 -> 24 a round, skipped turns about the same.
# TidalWave is left out (plans/team-angles-set.txt): it does not load on Robocode 1.11.2. Gains divide
# by 46 teams. A battle step's exit 1 (some battles failed) lets the card go on.
#   clprep  build aa, bb and cl (tmclear: CLEAR on every team, the named ones included)
#   clbb    bb vs aa, 45 teams x 12 seeds (base 7600), 10 rounds; clcl the same for cl
#   clff    own-fire read of both arms (tools/friendly_hits.py --candidate-only)
#   clsum   projected team APS change for cl = sum of its per-team gain less half of bb's / 46
#           (gate: +0.30 with the 95% low end above zero). The card changes nothing: on a PASS a PR
#           turns FORCE_CLEAR on.
# Each seed is a pair (the arm and aa): 2 x 45 x 12 x 2 = 2,160 battles, about 2.2 h at 12 workers
# (sizes itself to the host). Every step resumes where it stopped.
# Stop rules on every battle step (halt; every battle fought is kept and a rerun resumes): 60 failed
# battles (a broken jar, or the PC's burst of failures seen 2026-11-02), no battle in 30 minutes (a
# hung step), or 40+ skipped turns a battle over the last 100 (CLEAR's extra checks costing too
# much CPU). A halt in clbb leaves the rest of clbb and all 1,080 of clcl; in clcl, the rest of clcl.
# The team thread reads claude/pc-team-clear-results.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-team-clear        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-team-clear)
# Run it from master (one bench queue at a time):
#   git checkout master && git pull

set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set T = python3 tools/team_modes.py

clprep | git checkout -q master && V=$(sed -n 's:.*<robot.release>\(.*\)</robot.release>.*:\1:p' ../hadur-robot/pom.xml) && test -n "$V" && for j in aa bb cl; do rm -f bisect/hadur117.HadurTeam_"$V"$j.jar; done && rm -f ${OUT}/team-clear-*.md && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set team-census46.txt && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && bash ./build-ablation.sh bb && bash ./build-ablation.sh tmclear && mkdir -p work && for a in bb cl; do rm -rf work/team-clear-"$V"-$a && sed "s/@V@/$V/g" plans/team-clear-$a.args > work/team-clear-$a.args || exit 1; done && for j in aa bb cl; do test -f bisect/hadur117.HadurTeam_"$V"$j.jar || exit 1; done && mvn -q compile
clbb   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/team-clear-bb.args" || test $? -eq 1
  after: clprep
  watch: battles=1080
  stop: fails 60
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100
clcl   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/team-clear-cl.args" || test $? -eq 1
  after: clbb
  watch: battles=1080
  stop: fails 60
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100
clff   | V=$(sed -n 's:.*<robot.release>\(.*\)</robot.release>.*:\1:p' ../hadur-robot/pom.xml) && python3 tools/friendly_hits.py --candidate-only work/team-clear-"$V"-bb > ${OUT}/team-clear-friendly-bb.md && python3 tools/friendly_hits.py --candidate-only work/team-clear-"$V"-cl > ${OUT}/team-clear-friendly-cl.md
  after: clcl
clsum  | ${T} gate --report ${OUT}/team-clear-cl.md --control ${OUT}/team-clear-bb.md --seeds 12 --teams 46 --min-aps 0.3 --out-md ${OUT}/team-clear-verdict.md
  after: clff
clpr   | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-team-clear-results "Members out of their teammates' bullets (CLEAR): every team, 12 seeds" $(ls ${OUT}/team-clear-*.md 2>/dev/null)
  after: clsum
